  "date": "2026-08-14",
  "summary": "Every food-ontology entity page (leaf, group, category) across all 11 domains was migrated from a fact-table-only layout to a narrative-first educational reference layout. Authored catalog fields (summary, beginner_notes, faq, origin_context, introduction) that previously existed but never rendered are now published wherever present, at every tier (leaf, group, and category), and gracefully omitted (no placeholders, no empty sections) wherever absent.",
  "methodology": "Every leaf/group/category HTML page across all 11 food-ontology domains was checked programmatically against its source catalog entity: a 'rendered' count requires both the narrative section's markup AND the entity's own (HTML-escaped) authored text to be present in that specific page's HTML; a 'suppressed_no_data' count is a page correctly omitting a section because the catalog has no authored value for that field; 'empty_section_violations' counts any section markup rendered with no backing data (must be zero); 'duplicated_narrative_instances' counts any page where an authored text block appears more than once verbatim (must be zero). One authored FAQ answer per cheese entity that is byte-identical to that entity's summary is intentionally dropped by renderFAQ() to avoid shipping the same sentence twice on one page; this is a deliberate de-duplication decision, not a rendering defect \u2014 see architecture_notes.consolidation_decisions.",
