  },
  "publication_scope_note": "Cheese (204 leaf + 9 group + 1 category pages) was regenerated with the new architecture in dist/cheeses/, dist/cheese-groups/, dist/cheese-categories/ and passes full certification, but was NOT promoted to the live root (no root cheeses/ directory exists yet, consistent with its state before this phase). Publishing the cheese domain live is a separate go-live decision from a prior audit (AQ-01 navigation-review.md) outside AQ-02A's scope, which was to fix the renderer, not to newly launch a domain. All other 10 domains (protein/foods, fruit, vegetable, grain-starch, legume, nut-seed, herb-spice, sweet-flavor, sauce-condiment, fungi) were promoted to their live root paths.",
  "regression_verification": {
    "ontology_catalogs_changed": false,
    "runtime_artifacts_changed": false,
    "editorial_artifacts_changed": false,
    "wine_artifacts_changed": false,
    "governance_docs_changed": false,
    "changed_scope": [
      "lib/food-publication/narrative.js (new)",
      "lib/food-publication/pages.js (added narrative passthrough)",
      "lib/food-publication/projections.js (added narrative extraction)",
      "lib/taxonomy-render.js (added shared narrative-rendering helpers)",
      "lib/taxonomy-{protein-food,fruit,vegetable,grain-starch,legume,nut-seed,herb-spice,sweet-flavor,sauce-condiment,fungi,cheese}-render.js (new section architecture, all three tiers)",
      "data/generated/*-pages.json and data/pages/*-pages.json for all 11 domains (regenerated projections/page models carrying the new narrative field)",
      "dist/ and the 10 live root ingredient/group/category directories (regenerated HTML)",
      "root sitemap.xml / crawl-manifest.json / release-manifest.json (regenerated by the standard per-domain publish pipeline; incidentally now covers 10 of 11 domains instead of 1, since all 10 were regenerated in the same session \u2014 the remaining sitemap-index gap for cheese is a pre-existing AQ-01 finding, not newly introduced)",
      "reports/* publication pipeline reports (regenerated by the standard pipeline)"
    ],
    "verification_method": "git status diffed against data/*.json (catalog roots), data/runtime/, docs/, lib/editorial/, lib/runtime/, lib/publication/, and every lib/taxonomy-wine-*.js / taxonomy-descriptor*.js / taxonomy-grape*.js / taxonomy-pairing*.js file \u2014 all clean (zero changes) after the full 11-domain pipeline run."
  },
  "architecture_notes": {
    "shared_helpers_added": [
      "renderSummary()",
      "renderEducationalIntroduction()",
      "renderBeginnerGuide()",
      "renderFAQ()",
      "renderWinePairingExplanation()",
      "renderCommonCulinaryUses()",
      "renderRegionalContext()",
      "renderKnowledgeCards()",
      "renderNarrativeSection()",
      "renderNarrativeText()",
      "renderMetaLinkSection()",
      "renderCharacteristicsBlock()",
      "renderDefinitionList()",
      "renderOverviewRows()"
    ],
    "narrative_field_registry": "lib/food-publication/narrative.js defines NARRATIVE_FIELDS per tier (leaf/group/category), domain-agnostic by design \u2014 a new food domain's catalog automatically gets narrative rendering the moment it names its fields summary/beginner_notes/faq/seo_description/origin_context/introduction, with zero per-domain configuration required beyond calling the shared helpers already wired into every renderer.",
    "future_domain_guardrail": "Because narrative extraction lives in the shared projections/pages stage (not per-domain code) and every domain renderer is now a thin composition of the shared helpers in the order Hero -> narrative tier -> metadata tier, applied uniformly at leaf, group, AND category tiers, a new domain that copies an existing renderer file inherits the full educational-reference layout by construction. Shipping a fact-table-only page would now require a renderer to actively skip calling renderEducationalIntroduction()/renderWinePairingExplanation()/etc., not merely omit extra work.",
    "consolidation_decisions": [
